WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.333 --> 00:00:02.925
We took every element, tested it to the

2
00:00:02.925 --> 00:00:05.516
worst possible environment it could be in, and

3
00:00:05.516 --> 00:00:08.107
assured that it would work in that environment.

4
00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:13.359
That discipline matters in safety-critical software. Avionics certification

5
00:00:13.359 --> 00:00:18.051
can span years. Connect development, verification, documentation, and

6
00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:21.570
evidence, starting with the first draft.

7
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.155
The wage rate comes from U.S. labour data.

8
00:00:26.155 --> 00:00:29.810
This first-draft model compares three hundred twenty hours

9
00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:33.465
with eight. That is about twenty thousand four

10
00:00:33.465 --> 00:00:37.120
hundred dollars of drafting capacity. Review, target testing,

11
00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:38.948
and approval remain separate.

12
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.807
Noyce IDE connects an end-to-end, AI-assisted certification workflow,

13
00:00:44.807 --> 00:00:49.613
with local models inside an air-gapped installation. Engineers

14
00:00:49.613 --> 00:00:51.415
review the outputs.

15
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.068
Take a motor controller. Its two opposing outputs

16
00:00:56.068 --> 00:00:59.137
must never be active together. Start with the

17
00:00:59.137 --> 00:01:02.205
circuit and its registers, then carry that constraint

18
00:01:02.205 --> 00:01:05.273
into a software requirement. That requirement becomes a

19
00:01:05.273 --> 00:01:08.341
thread through the engineering work, connecting the physical

20
00:01:08.341 --> 00:01:11.410
intent to the checks that follow. Recover the

21
00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:14.478
architecture to understand dependencies, and trace the requirement

22
00:01:14.478 --> 00:01:17.546
into its implementation and tests. Now a change

23
00:01:17.546 --> 00:01:20.614
has context: you can see what it affects,

24
00:01:20.614 --> 00:01:23.683
what supports it, and which links still need

25
00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:24.066
attention.

26
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.328
With that context in place, inspect static analysis

27
00:01:29.328 --> 00:01:32.656
findings and review a proposed patch before staging

28
00:01:32.656 --> 00:01:35.984
it. The suggestion is only a starting point;

29
00:01:35.984 --> 00:01:39.312
the engineer decides what changes. Then examine decision

30
00:01:39.312 --> 00:01:42.640
coverage and use bounded checks to investigate properties

31
00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:45.968
and counterexamples. Resource budgets add another constraint, so

32
00:01:45.968 --> 00:01:49.296
inspect Flash, RAM, and stack estimates alongside build

33
00:01:49.296 --> 00:01:52.624
changes. If the target faults, decode the exception

34
00:01:52.624 --> 00:01:55.952
frame and fault registers to guide the investigation.

35
00:01:55.952 --> 00:01:59.280
Each view contributes a different part of the

36
00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:02.608
engineering picture. Review the findings together, because a

37
00:02:02.608 --> 00:02:05.520
passing test alone cannot explain every failure.

38
00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:14.655
Noyce takes the project through a connected pipeline.

39
00:02:14.655 --> 00:02:18.311
AI agents prepare lifecycle-document drafts from project context,

40
00:02:18.311 --> 00:02:21.966
while verification and audit records stay with the

41
00:02:21.966 --> 00:02:25.622
work. Engineers review the drafts, resolve open items,

42
00:02:25.622 --> 00:02:29.277
and issue a versioned baseline. The workflow assembles

43
00:02:29.277 --> 00:02:32.933
the supporting evidence into an engineering review package.

44
00:02:32.933 --> 00:02:36.588
Inspect each compliance objective against the records, identify

45
00:02:36.588 --> 00:02:40.243
remaining gaps, and keep the next action visible.

46
00:02:40.243 --> 00:02:43.899
Automation prepares the material; the project team owns

47
00:02:43.899 --> 00:02:45.270
review and acceptance.

48
00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:53.651
The first draft is just the start. Connect

49
00:02:53.651 --> 00:02:56.802
the certification workflow end to end, with Noyce

50
00:02:56.802 --> 00:02:57.195
IDE.
